{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790266732,"nonce":"nqBxQQG+RHz089z+DxSDGipUGGk=","title":"Python: * and + on a boxed array treat it as a list","message":"Reproduces on main dea6d08b (~/bin-main/zypy on the NUC):\n\n    from array import array\n    def ident(x):\n        return x\n    print(ident([1]), ident(\"s\"))\n    b = ident(array(\"B\", [2, 3]))\n    print(b + array(\"B\", [9]))\n    print(b * 2)\n\nCPython prints array('B', [2, 3, 9]) and array('B', [2, 3, 2, 3]). zypy prints the list [2, 3, 9] for the concat, and the repeat raises \"TypeError: unsupported operand type(s): 'list' and 'int'\". A dynamic array slice now returns an array, so the same happens to `data[a:b] * 2` on a dynamic value. Found while verifying p4-rebind-slices-json.","files":null}]}